>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `FASTFORCE_TAC`

``` hol4
clasimpLib.FASTFORCE_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by depth-first classical search with simplification.

`FASTFORCE_TAC thms` runs the classical fast search driver after installing
assumption-aware full simplification as an unsafe wrapper. It uses the
current claset and clasimpset and has no numeric search bound, so it can
diverge.

Unmarked theorems are inserted as assumptions. Use explicit classical
markers for temporary claset rules, `Simp` for a temporary rewrite, and
`Iff` for a temporary iff declaration. Generic simplifier markers are
passed to the wrapper.

### Failure

Fails unless depth-first search closes the goal. Search can diverge.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem fastforce_tac_example:
  (p \/ q) ==> (p ==> r) ==> (q ==> r) ==> r
Proof
  clasimpLib.FASTFORCE_TAC []
QED
```

